From 2431eb3adcd2e69b6bb19af02d3bf890067db76b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: CipherScope <dev@cipherscope.io>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 08:33:15 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 44/48] test: add feature_p2mr_mldsa44.py

On regtest with -testactivationheight=p2mr_mldsa44@N, with a second node
that runs -acceptnonstdtxn=1:

- the mempool refuses a validly signed S1 spend while the next block is
  N-1 and takes it once the next block is N;
- a block below N takes a spend with an invalid signature;
- a reorganization back below N removes the template spend, a
  non-template spend the second node took, and their children;
- after activation S1 and S2 spends relay and confirm, and eight kinds
  of invalid spend fail both in the mempool and in a block, including
  SIGHASH_SINGLE without an output and a public key one byte short;
- only the templates at depth one or more may carry signature chunks
  over 80 bytes, and a single leaf tree is spent without a signature;
- one transaction spends P2MR ML-DSA-44, P2MR Schnorr and P2TR inputs.
